He's been in there quite a while.

295
00:15:59,876 --> 00:16:03,296
Well, if the topic is science, he can be a really chatty Patty.

296
00:16:03,505 --> 00:16:04,548
I'm bored.

297
00:16:04,756 --> 00:16:06,675
Me, too. Hey.

298
00:16:07,008 --> 00:16:09,469
Someday somebody's gonna write a book about Sheldon.

299
00:16:09,761 --> 00:16:15,100
Don't you want there to be a chapter about how loving and supportive you two were?

300
00:16:15,308 --> 00:16:17,227
Doesn't matter. I ain't reading it.

301
00:16:20,063 --> 00:16:21,940
This is groundbreaking work.

302
00:16:22,149 --> 00:16:23,859
Thank you. And...?

303
00:16:24,568 --> 00:16:25,318
And...?

304
00:16:25,527 --> 00:16:27,779
I thought you might want to apologize.

305
00:16:28,071 --> 00:16:29,071
Well...

306
00:16:29,156 --> 00:16:30,156
Why?

307
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:32,784
You tried to shut me up with a patch.

308
00:16:33,201 --> 00:16:35,579
Well... I-I give those to everyone.

309
00:16:35,787 --> 00:16:44,212
A-And you have to understand, Sheldon, that while your math is-is theoretically correct, we don't have the technical capability to execute it.

310
00:16:44,421 --> 00:16:45,839
So I'm ahead of my time?

311
00:16:46,465 --> 00:16:49,509
Well... it would appear so.

312
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:52,304
All right, call me when you catch up.

313
00:16:53,138 --> 00:16:53,763
Uh...

314
00:16:53,972 --> 00:16:55,223
We can go now.

315
00:17:00,812 --> 00:17:01,812
♪ j” rocket...

